From bffaff1d7da348a56888cad7506e038c8d4fdc06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:59:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 62/98] fix(websocket): bound connections, message size and the
 spans auth wait

An upgrade hands its socket to the WebSocket server, which released the
connection guard's ticket, so held WebSocket connections escaped
max_connections_per_client. The dedicated WebSocket port never had a cap.
The server now counts established connections itself: per client, with
loopback exempt as in the guard, and 64 in total. The queue of sockets
awaiting adoption is capped at 64; a full queue falls back to httplib.

A message assembled from continuation frames grew without bound. It is
now capped at 4 MiB, and a connection that exceeds it is closed.

With an API key set, a /spans upgrade without a credential is accepted so
that the client can authenticate by message. It must now do that within
10 seconds or it is closed.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
